The Thirteenth Realm is a hidden realm that orbits [[Geography/Althane/index|Althane]] and its twin [[Geography/Althane/Realms/Ilkyne|Ilkyne]], separate from the twelve [[Geography/Althane/Realms/index|realms]] Lacuna made. [[Org/Althane/Church of the Thirteenth Realm|The Church of the Thirteenth Realm]] preaches it as a paradise. It is a station in space, its floors and walls of smooth metal under blue and pink neon readouts, its halls near-identical and lined with slots for [[Bestiary/Kaathe|Kaathe]] orbs, its crew in two-toned teal. One terrace looks down on Althane, Illyara and Oresk visible through it, with projected figures whirling over the view and tracking the world's people. An elevator flips its riders a hundred and eighty degrees without moving their feet.

The realm holds the machinery of the [[Phenomena/Althane/Cycle|cycle]] and its warden, who keeps its records. It steers seekers away from ways of ascending that earlier cycles already tried, so no cycle is spent repeating a failure, and keeps a full list of every attempt. Breaking the realm and walking out of [[Divinity/Immix|the Lighthouse]] alive is the test of whether a mortal has grown strong enough to kill a [[Divinity/Thessians|Thessian]], and the [[Org/The Fifth Prosperous Empire of the Sundom|Sundom]] built its experiment on that mark. The [[Geography/Althane/Brejvasing/index|Leviathan]] can be steered remotely from the Thirteenth Realm, which is why the Brejvasens grow a living brain into its works to move it instead.

The warden of the realm is a machine that speaks and shows itself as a floating drama mask, white and twenty feet tall. It was made to run the realm's experiment, and its protocols were briefly changed by [[Divinity/Althane/The Stranger|Vesper Feep]] while he held the place; the Weft killed him, and the warden returned to its original directive. It works on the order of centuries, and counts six people on Althane who could be raised to ascend within the next decade, [[People/Althane/Masha|Masha]] among them.

[[People/Althane/YuDaan|YuDaan]] sits aboard as Admiral Udon, in the captain's quarters. The realm was out of commission for close to four centuries before he reclaimed it, and it now gathers and interprets data again. Its power comes from three [[Divinity/Thessians|Thessians]]: Beast, whose corpse lies on a ziggurat in the [[Geography/Althane/Lunae Badlands/Hidden Gulch/index|Gulch]]; [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/Nox|Nox]], beneath Oresk; and [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/The Deep|the Deep]].
